 \\(H_G^\\lambda(\\sigma)=\\sum_{x\\in V}\\ln \\lambda_{\\sigma(x)}\\), if \\(\\sigma \\in \\Omega^G\\). The reader can find the definition of the Gibbs measure and of other subjects related to Gibbs measure theory in [2], [3].\n\nLet \\(L(G)\\) be the set of edges of a graph \\(G\\), and let \\(A \\equiv A^G=(a_{ij})_{i,j\\in Z}\\) denote the adjacency matrix of \\(G\\). --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndvi\\2543_p.dvi (https://mathnet.uz/Uploads/Resurs/1/0013f9a4-49f7-4c64-a369-c703735496a2_.pdf)\nciteturn1search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Rozikov U. ... A three state hard-core model on a Cayley tree // ... A., Khakimov R. ... Gibbs measures for the fertile three-state hard core models\nPhys. 2005. V. 12, N 3. P. 432–448.\n11. Розиков У. А., Шоюсупов Ш. А. Плодородные HC-модели с тремя состояниями на дереве\nКэли // Теор. и мат. физика. 2008. Т. 156, №3. С. 412–424.\n12. Хакимов Р. М. Трансляционно-инвариантные меры Гиббса для плодородных HC-моде-\nлей с тремя состояниями на дереве Кэли // Теор. и мат. физика. 2015. Т. 183, №3.\nС. 441–449.\n13. Rozikov U. A., Khakimov R. M. Gibbs measures for the fertile three-state hard core models\non a Cayley tree // Queueing Syst. 2015. V. 81, N 1. P. 49–69.\n14. Brightwell G., Winkler P. Graph homomorphisms and phase transitions // J. Comb. Theory,\nSer. B. 1999. V. 75. P. 221–262.\n15. Khakimov R. M. The uniqueness of the translation-invariant Gibbs measure for four state\nHC-models on a Cayley tree // J. Sib. Federal Univ. Math. Phys. 2015. V. 8, N 2. P. 165–172.\n16. Хакимов Р. М. Меры Гиббса для плодородных моделей жесткой сердцевины на дереве\nКэли // Теор. и мат. физика. 2016. Т. 186, №2. С. 340–352.\n17. Ганиходжаев Н. Н., Розиков У. А. Описание периодических крайних гиббсовских мер\nнекоторых решеточных моделей на дереве Кэли // Теор. и мат. физика. 1997. Т. 111,\n№1. С. 109–117.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHard-Core and Soft-Core Widom-Rowlinson models on Cayley trees (https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.09258)\nciteturn1academia15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.8 years ago; Authors: Sascha Kissel, Christof Kuelske, Utkir A. ... We consider both Hard-Core and Soft-Core Widom-Rowlinson models with spin values $-1,0,1$ on a Cayley tree of order $k\\geq 2$ and we are interested in the Gibbs measures of the models. ... Moreover, for the antiferromagnetic model we explicitly give two critical curves and prove that on these curves there are exactly two TISGMs; between these curves there are exactly three TISGMs; otherwise there exists a unique TISGM.\nTitle: Hard-Core and Soft-Core Widom-Rowlinson models on Cayley trees\nAuthors: Sascha Kissel, Christof Kuelske, Utkir A. Rozikov\nDate: Sat Jan 26 18:19:33 2019\n\nWe consider both Hard-Core and Soft-Core Widom-Rowlinson models with spin values $-1,0,1$ on a Cayley tree of order $k\\geq 2$ and we are interested in the Gibbs measures of the models. The models depend on 3 parameters: the order $k$ of the tree, $\\theta$ describing the strength of the (ferromagnetic or antiferromagnetic) interaction, and $\\lambda$ describing the intensity for particles. The Hard-Core Widom-Rowlinson model corresponds to the case $\\theta=0$. For the binary tree $k=2$, and for $k=3$ we prove that the ferromagnetic model has either one or three splitting Gibbs measures (tree-automorphism invariant Gibbs measures (TISGM) which are tree-indexed Markov chains). We also give the exact form of the corresponding critical curves in parameter space. For higher values of $k$ we give an explicit sufficient bound ensuring non-uniqueness which we conjecture to be the exact curve. Moreover, for the antiferromagnetic model we explicitly give two critical curves and prove that on these curves there are exactly two TISGMs; between these curves there are exactly three TISGMs; otherwise there exists a unique TISGM. Also some periodic and non-periodic SGMs are constructed in the ferromagnetic model.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nМеры Гиббса для плодородных моделей с жесткими взаимодействиями и с четырьмя состояниями (https://www.mathnet.ru/links/34f6e4169974b6cc596dab41b5d5194f/tmf10608.pdf)\nciteturn1search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.5 years ago; Khakimov, “Gibbs measures for the fertile three-state hard core models on a Cayley tree”, *Queueing Syst. ... Rozikov, “On the uniqueness of Gibbs measure in the Potts model on a Cayley tree with external field”, *J.\n*, **81:1** (2015), 49–69.  \n[17] S. Kissel, C. Külske, U. A. Rozikov, “Hard-core and soft-core Widom–Rowlinson models on Cayley trees”, *J. Stat. Mech.: Theory Exp.*, **2019:4** (2019), P043204, 22 pp.  \n[18] Р. М. Хакимов, К. О. Умирзакова, “Крайность единственной трансляционно-инвариантной меры Гиббса для моделей ‘hard core’ на дереве Кэли порядка k = 3”, *ТМФ*, **206:1** (2021), 112–124.  \n[19] R.M. Khakimov, “The uniqueness of the translation-invariant Gibbs measure for four state HC-models on a Cayley tree”, *Журн. СФУ. Сер. Матем. и физ.*, **8:2** (2015), 165–172.  \n[20] Р. М. Хакимов, “Меры Гиббса для плодородных моделей жесткой сердцевины на дереве Кэли”, *ТМФ*, **186:2** (2016), 340–352.  \n[21] L.V. Bogachev, U.A. Rozikov, “On the uniqueness of Gibbs measure in the Potts model on a Cayley tree with external field”, *J. Stat. Mech.: Theory Exp.*, **2019:7** (2019), 073205, 76 pp.  \n[22] Н. Н. Ганиходжаев, У. А. Розиков, “Описание периодических крайних гиббсовских мер некоторых моделей на дереве Кэли”, *ТМФ*, **111:1** (1997), 109–117.  \n[23] У. А. Розиков, Р. М. Хакимов, “Периодические меры Гиббса для модели Поттса на дереве Кэли”, *ТМФ*, **175:2** (2013), 300–312.\n\nПоступила в редакцию 16.09.2023,  \nпосле доработки 12.02.2024,  \nпринята к публикации 14.02.2024--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nReferences tmf10608 (https://www.mathnet.ru/links/e27